%description:

TcpSpoof.seqNo:iss -- the segment carries the ISS of the clock, 250000 at 1 s.

The claim (TcpSpoof.ned): "Sends fabricated TCP packets. ... Compatible with both IPv4
(~Ipv4) and IPv6 (~Ipv6)." TcpSpoof::sendSpoofPacket() sends one segment at the time t: a
header of 20 bytes without options and data, with the window 16384, no ACK, and the SYN bit
of isSYN.

The claim (TcpSpoof.ned): "Sequence number (-1 for TCP ISS)".

The classes: iss (-1: the number comes from the clock, as the ISS of TCP: 250000 for each
second, modulo 2^32) and value (another number: the segment carries it). The code:
TcpSpoof::sendSpoofPacket() calls chooseInitialSeqNum() for -1. This test separates "iss" from the other class. This test fails: chooseInitialSeqNum() calls
fmod() with simTime() * 250000.0, so the modulus 2^32 + 1 becomes a simtime_t too, which the
time scale of the run cannot hold; the run stops with "simtime_t: Cannot represent
4.29497e+09" (finding PF-13).

Node under test: host1; host1 has TcpSpoof in place of its TCP and no application. The spoof sends one segment at 1 s
from the port 5000 to host2:1000 with the sequence number 12345 and the SYN bit, unless the
test changes one of these values. The tap drops the segment after host1 sends
it: the TCP of a receiver cannot take a segment of TcpSpoof (finding PF-11). Observation: level 1, the segment carries the sequence number
250000.

%# parameter: TcpSpoof.seqNo
%# class: iss
%# value: -1
%# key: *.host1.tcp.seqNo
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSpoofSeqNoIss")
        .intercept(tap("tap").filterPacket("tcp.srcPort == 5000")
                     .drop()
                     .describe("the segment of the spoof: the TCP of a receiver cannot take it (PF-11)"))
        .once(on("host1.eth[0].mac").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.srcPort == 5000 && tcp.sequenceNo == 250000")
             .describe("the segment of the spoof, with the sequence number 250000")
             .within(1.1));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSpoofSeqNoIss compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.seqNo = -1    # the parameter under test
*.host1.tcp.typename = "TcpSpoof"
*.host1.numApps = 0
*.host1.tcp.srcAddress = ""
*.host1.tcp.destAddress = "host2"
*.host1.tcp.srcPort = 5000
*.host1.tcp.destPort = 1000
*.host1.tcp.seqNo = 12345
*.host1.tcp.isSYN = true
*.host1.tcp.t = 1s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSpoofSeqNoIss: PASS
